========================================================================
VERDICT
========================================================================

## **REJECT** walker vs guard parity

Assigned question: **Does stmt `println` miss any shape that free-call
`eprintln` catches?**

**YES.** Live emit-c on the product host:

| Shape (after `// SECRET: tok`) | stmt `println` | free-call `eprintln` |
|--------------------------------|----------------|----------------------|
| `(("x") + tok)` grouping then `+` | **FN** rc=0, emits `oo_print_str(oo_str_concat((oo_str_lit("x")), tok))` | **BLOCK** `ERR	secret	eprintln sink refuses SECRET tok` |
| `((1) + tok)` int grouping then `+` | **FN** rc=0, emits `oo_print_int(((1LL) + tok))` | **BLOCK** same secret |
| `f(g(), tok)` nested call, secret after inner `RPAREN` | **FN** rc=0, emits `oo_print_str(f(g(), tok))` | **BLOCK** same secret |
| `"x".len() + tok` method `RPAREN` then `+` | **FN** rc=0 (stmt walk stops at first `RPAREN`) | **BLOCK** same secret |

Root cause: stmt `println` is special-cased (`c_emit_ident.oo` L129–131
→ `c_emit_print.oo`). Its IDENT scan **stops at the first `COMMA` /
`RPAREN` / `SEMI` with no paren depth**. Free-call `eprintln` is **not**
special-cased: `c_emit_expr_c` → `c_secret_emit_guard` →
`c_guard_scan_idents` on the **full lowered C args**, which still sees
`tok` after a nested `)`.

`check_secret_println_sinks` (`c_emit_secret.oo` L175–193) has the
**same first-`RPAREN` stop** for **both** names. So `oodac check` is
FN on these shapes for both (parity of a hole). emit-c still runs that
front-door first; when it misses, **only** the eprintln guard saves
the sink. Stmt println then **prints the SECRET ident**.

Do **not** ACCEPT 2.9 parity from `s29_println_guard_smoke.sh` (bare
IDENT + string no-FP only). Do **not** treat Peer 1 “assigned FN=0”
as this OWN — Peer 1 did not probe grouping/`RPAREN`-before-SECRET.

