Minimal recreate (grouping hole):

```
// SECRET: tok
pub fn main() {
    let tok = "s";
    println(("x") + tok);   # emit-c FN
    # eprintln(("x") + tok);  # emit-c BLOCK
}
```

========================================================================
WHAT STILL HAS PARITY (do not over-claim the REJECT)
========================================================================

Bare IDENT, top-level multi-arg, ungrouped concat, simple `wrap(tok)` /
`id(id(tok))`, string-lit no-FP, callee-alias, and expr-position
`println` all **BLOCK or ALLOW together**. Official fixtures and the
s29 smoke stay green. Peer 1 assigned matrix staying green is
**compatible** with this REJECT: those shapes never put a `RPAREN`
between the sink LPAREN and the SECRET IDENT.

`println(g(), tok)` (secret as a **later top-level** arg after an empty
call) is emit-c BLOCK on stmt println because after `c_emit_expr_c`
consumes `g()`, the **next** arg scan sees `tok`. Check still FN both.
That is **not** a stmt miss vs eprintln.

========================================================================
NAMED RESIDUALS (not this REJECT)
========================================================================

R1. **Check front-door** is FN on the same `RPAREN` class for **both**
    names. Dual-path secret is **emit-only** for eprintln. Fixing only
    stmt println does not close `oodac check`.
R2. **emit-llvm** has no `c_guard_scan_idents`. Hole shapes ALLOW on
    both names. LLVM `print` alias already named in `s71_security.oot` R2.
R3. **2.9 unify still OPEN** (Peer 1 REJECT of the helper land). This
    audit’s REJECT is the **parity FN**, not only “call site missing.”
R4. DE2.9 table (`c_emit_secret.oo:175-186` → `c_secret_emit_guard`) is
    still the old token walk. Guard wants C `args`, not toks.
R5. `${}` / `#[Secret]` / full IFC — 5.8 / SECRET_TAINT. Not this OWN.
R6. 6.1 `env_set` check type-first on this host — `s61_*`. Not 2.9.
R7. `println((tok))` check TYPE “expects at least 1 argument” (inner
    `RPAREN` stolen as closer). eprintln check still SECRET. Separate
    arity-desync; not required for this REJECT.

