========================================================================
FINAL
========================================================================

**REJECT** 2.9 walker vs guard parity. Stmt `println` **does** miss
shapes that free-call `eprintln` catches: any SECRET IDENT that appears
**after a nested `RPAREN` still inside the sink args**. Live emit-c
prints `tok`. The eprintln guard refuses the same source. Bare-IDENT
smoke is not a substitute for this rail.

Fix (not this worker): stop special-casing stmt `println`, **or** give
`c_emit_println` a depth-aware scan / `c_secret_emit_guard` on joined
arg text; **and** make the check walker depth-aware (or it stays FN).

